  "body": "A small plate that came off my machine this week, driven end to end through camcraft v0.14.0: model in, 2D operations in the GUI, verify, then posted with the built-in Tormach PathPilot post. The program ran clean on my LinuxCNC control.\n\nFinished:\n\n![finished plate](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbrasselle/Camcraft/showcase-assets/showcase/IMG_4887.jpg)\n\nOn the machine:\n\n![on the machine](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbrasselle/Camcraft/showcase-assets/showcase/IMG_4888.jpg)\n\n![on the machine, other side](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbrasselle/Camcraft/showcase-assets/showcase/IMG_4891.jpg)\n\nI single-blocked the first run and everything matched the project. camcraft is in my toolchain for plates like this now.\n\nOne wish that came out of the setup: side views keep the perspective projection, so the part never looks \"straight\" when lining it up - filed as #434 (orthographic viewport projection).\n",
